From 430a8d44641a851ee36b4a18582a8a321d7c7c90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:39:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): sample the hub CPU advisory on its own thread,
 not across sync rounds [daveey]

91511fad split the advisory CPU sample across sync-loop iterations: snapshot A after one
round, B after the next, then the strict 1000-2000 ms window check. A hub round takes 3-20 s
(board pulls plus feed wakes), so every finish was dropped (cpu_sample_drops climbing, zero
records), cache/hub-cpu-sample.json aged past 15 s and every hub claim deferred
hub_cpu_unknown with 0/9 slots in use (hermes-hub, 2026-11-12 07:12-07:16Z, until a user
service stopgap took over the sampling).

Fix: hermes_cli/machine_cpu_sampler.AdvisorySampler takes a full cpu.sample() (two
/proc/stat snapshots ~1 s apart, blocking only its own thread) every 5 windows (5 s) while
the root limit is on, and writes each valid one to the advisory file. The sync loop starts it
and closes it in a finally, so a stopped loop still lets the advisory go stale (fail-closed).
The Reporter no longer measures: it takes the sampler's newest sample at most once (never
replayed), only when measured under the same limit and <= 10 s old. The pending-wake clamp in
the loop and the unused begin/finish primitives are removed.

Detection: hermes_cli/kanban_hub_cpu_alert.check runs once per embedded-dispatcher tick.
When the root limit is on and the advisory has been unusable (>15 s, missing or malformed)
for 60 s of this process's own observation, it opens ONE card per incident
(idempotency_key hub-cpu-advisory-stale) naming the sample age and the sampler counters; a
fresh sample ends the incident; a later one comments on the open card (hourly at most) or
opens a new card once that one is done.

Proof:
- RED on origin/main ee3cb1f4ca: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_slow_round_cpu.py (real
  _run_forever + real Reporter + real cpu.sample window check over /proc/stat, window scaled
  to 200-400 ms, rounds that outlast it) fails "advisory not written while the sync round
  ran: 0 records". GREEN here, 3/3 repeat runs.
- Mutants killed: dropping sampler.close() in the loop's finally (slow-round test), letting
  the Reporter take a sample with the gate off (test_machine_metrics).
- hermes-core-wt test: 34 kanban-sync/metrics/admission files 735 passed; 53 gateway
  dispatcher/watcher files 772 passed. scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
